      "textEn": "\nDharmasutra; Samah—equal; Tatah—from that; Dyumatsena—Dyumatsena; Atha—thereafter; Sumatih—Sumati; Subala—Subala; Janita—will be born;\nTatah—thereafter.. From Marjari, Shrutashrava; from Shrutashrava, Yutayu;\nFrom Yutayu, Nirmitra; from Nirmitra, Sunakshatra; from Sunakshatra, Brihatsen; from Brihatsen, Karmajit; from Karmajit,\nSutanjay; from Sutanjay, Vipra; from Vipra, Shuchi; from Shuchi, Kshem; from Kshem, Suvrat; from Suvrat, Dharmasutra; from Dharmasutra,\nSam; from Sam, Dyumatsen; from Dyumatsen, Sumati; and from Sumati, a son named Subala will be born. Sunitha: Satyajith Vishwajit Driipunjay. Barhadratha and the king, Bhavya, with a thousand years of courage. 49. Meaning of the word\n\nSunitha: - Sunitha will be produced from Subala; Satyajit: - Satyajit; Atha: - From that; Vishwajit: - Vishwajit; Yat: - From that; Ripunjaya: - Ripunjaya;\nBarhadratha: - In the lineage of Brihadratha; Cha: - Also; Bhupala: - All the kings; Bhavya: - Will be; Sahasra-vatsaram: - For a thousand years\nContinuously.\nFrom Subal, Sunitha; from Sunitha, Satyajit; from Satyajit, Vishwajit; and from Vishwajit, Ripunjay will be born.\nWill be. All these men will be of the Brihadratha lineage, and they will rule the world for a thousand years. Meaning: This is the history of the aforementioned kings who ruled the earth for a thousand years, starting from Jarasandha. In this way, under the ninth canto of the Srimad Bhagavatam, the twenty-second chapter titled \"The Descendants of Ajamid\""
