a, it started raining. Thereafter, Rishyasringa performed a Putra-Yagya (sacrifice for a son) for King Dasharatha.\nBecause he had no son. From this, King Dasharatha had a son. By the grace of Rishyasringa,\nRomapada had a son named Chaturanga, and from Chaturanga, Prithulaksha was born. Brihadratho, Brihatkarma, Brihatbhanuscha, Tatasutah. Aadyadbhrnamanasastasmajjayadratha udahrutah. 11. Meaning of the word\n\nBrihadratha - Brihadratha; Brihatkarma - Brihatkarma; Brihatbhanu - Brihatbhanu; Cha - also; Tat - his son; Aadyat - the eldest;\nFrom Brihadratha; Brihannamaha - Brihannamaha was born; Tasmat - from that; Jayadratha - Jayadratha; Udahrutah - became famous as his son..\nPrithulaksha's sons were Brihadratha, Brihatkarma and Brihatbhanu. The eldest son, Brihadratha, had a son named Brihadmana.\nAnd from Brihadmana, Jayadratha was born."
